KZ2 patch 2181: a pipeline record with a boot-time prewarm; background builds
only once the record exists.

Written for the Pyrrhus native Mac bring-up; no game code or RPCS3 code used.
Licence: MIT (project LICENSE).

The archive of 2173 misses the engine's descriptors (the menu pipelines missed
on a warm file), so a session still rebuilt its known set -- synchronously, on
the drawing thread (the freezes seen in play), or in the background (the
missing menu boxes and gameplay elements seen in play: a dropped first draw of content drawn
only during the build window has no second chance).

The record keeps each new pipeline's full inputs beside the archive: the two
decompiled programs, the render state, the vertex layout, the formats. At boot
the workers rebuild the recorded set (PS3RECOMP_METAL_PSO_PREWARM_MAX, default
256, four workers, well inside a boot), so the menu and known gameplay draw
with their real pipelines before they are first needed. The default is
synchronous until the record exists -- a first play renders everything, slowly
-- and background after, because everything known is then prebuilt. An explicit
PS3RECOMP_METAL_ASYNC_PSO always wins. The port defaults the record path beside
the archive; the record file is generated at run time and never committed.

